@startuml orchestrator_class
title plogic - Orchestrator stage

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

interface UI {
}

class Orchestrator {
  +{static} evaluate(source: str, simplify: bool): Result<List<Evaluation>, List<Error>>
  +{static} simplify(source: str): Result<List<Simplification>, List<Error>>
  +{static} report(error: Error): str
}

class Evaluation {
  +table: TruthTable
  +simplification: Simplification?
}

class Token

class Scanner
class Parser
class ScanState
class ParseState
class Simplifier
class Simplification
class Step
class Interpreter
class TruthTable
class InfixPrinter
abstract class Expression
enum Error

note bottom of Orchestrator
  Stateless: pure composition of the pipeline
  scan -> parse -> per proposition (simplify ->
  choose expression -> interpret). Failure is always
  signalled by Result, with Err = List<Error>.

  Stage gates: a scan failure stops before parsing,
  a parse failure stops before simplification, and
  an EvalError stops the whole run. Steps 6-9 repeat
  once per parsed proposition.

  Step 8 tabulates the simplified expression by
  default, or the original with --no-simplificar.
  simplify() stops after simplification, returns each
  Simplification (expression and steps) and builds no
  tables, so no size limit applies (--simplificar).
  evaluate() returns one Evaluation per proposition:
  the table plus the Simplification when it ran, so
  the CLI can print the process with -m. It adds each
  table's display text through TruthTable.with_display:
  the tabulated expression in the label and, when
  simplification ran, the simplified formula in
  canonical order (InfixPrinter). report() is a pure
  formatter for the CLI. All three take their owned
  argument by value (ADR-044, ADR-046, ADR-047).
end note

UI --> Orchestrator

Orchestrator ..> Scanner : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Parser : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Simplifier : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Interpreter : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> TruthTable : with_display
Orchestrator ..> Evaluation : <<create>>
Evaluation --> TruthTable : table
Evaluation --> Simplification : simplification
Orchestrator ..> InfixPrinter : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Expression : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Error : <<use>>

Scanner ..> ScanState
Parser ..> ParseState
ScanState --> Token
ParseState --> Token
Interpreter ..> TruthTable : <<create>>
UI ..> TruthTable : <<use>>

@enduml
